Speed [SimTalk] - Turnplate
Sets the speed, with which the Turnplate designated by <Path> transports the MU, while it is located on
the plate.
Remarks
Specify -1 for an infinite speed.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Speed:speed
Watchable
The attribute is watchable.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type speed.
Note
In SimTalk 2.0 you can specify the speed units mps, fps, kmh, and mph.
Type in the unit directly after the number, without a separating blank space, for example 100kmh or
100.5kmh.
var len := 1.0ft
var s : speed := 10.5m / 1:30
var x : length := 3m
Speed [SimTalk] - Turnplate
11-2432 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
In SimTalk 2.0 you can enter the unit s for seconds. Enter the unit s directly after the number, without
a separating blank space. Entering the unit sometimes is necessary to make sure that the computed
expression has the correct data type.
var x : length := 10m
var s : speed := x / 2s   // Beware: x/2 would have the wrong unit, m 
instead of m/s
Example
MyTurnplate.Speed := 1.5
See also
Speed [text box] - Turnplate
